Subject: [PATCH 35/43] [3.1.1] [M156] [canvas2d] Resolve context filter before
 obtaining PaintCanvas and state

Original change's description:
> [canvas2d] Resolve context filter before obtaining PaintCanvas and state
>
> Canvas2DRecorderContext::Draw() and beginLayerImpl() currently resolve
> an unresolved context filter via StateGetFilter() inside
> ShouldUseCompositedDraw(), CompositedDraw(), and SaveLayerForState()
> while holding a raw PaintCanvas pointer/reference and a
> CanvasRenderingContext2DState reference.
>
> Because CanvasRenderingContext2DState::GetFilter() calls
> Document::UpdateStyleAndLayout() when resolving a CSS url() filter, a
> synchronous style and layout update can run scripts and resize or reset
> the canvas, destroying the recorder and invalidating the active
> PaintCanvas and CanvasRenderingContext2DState mid-draw.
>
> Resolve any unresolved context filter in Draw() and beginLayerImpl()
> before calling GetOrCreatePaintCanvas() and GetState(), and only query
> StateGetFilter() in CompositedDraw() and SaveLayerForState() when the
> filter is already resolved.
>
